// The lean water — the first slide where running out of matter is what stops you.
//
// `soup.ron` in every respect but one: the structural monomer is seeded at the cliff instead of
// two orders of magnitude above it. Everything else — size, seed, light, still water, the other
// two chemicals — is the control's, so a difference between the two slides is that one number.
//
//   mm-cli run scenarios/the_lean_water.ron --genome genomes/ancestor.mm --ticks 50000 --check
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- why this slide exists
//
// `docs/ECONOMY.md` §3 measured what a saturated soup actually runs out of, and it is none of the
// things the design intended. 128,000 units of structural carbon sit in cells and 1,379,000 are
// still dissolved: **the population consumes 8% of the one resource the design calls conserved
// and limiting.** What stops it is `split_pressure` — thirty divisions a tick refused for want of
// anywhere to put a daughter. The carrying capacity is a packing number.
//
// That is the single most consequential fact in the economy, because a contest over *area* is won
// by whoever turns matter into daughters fastest, which is whoever carries least. It is why
// §9a can scale the whole organelle catalogue fourfold and change the evolved loadout not at all:
// when space is the limit, earning more buys nothing, so no organelle can pay for itself however
// it is priced. Every "this mechanism pays nowhere" result in the panel rests on it.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- and why 10, not 200 or 40
//
// `docs/CHEMISTRY.md` §6 swept the seeding and found the population **flat across the top
// forty-fold and then a cliff** — so halving the soup changes nothing, and so does taking a tenth
// of it. That much still holds. Its numbers do not: the sweep predates the tempo pass of
// `616c445`, which halved growth and throughput, and **the cliff has moved up and got steeper.**
// Re-measured here, eight founders, 20,000 ticks, mutation off:
//
//     units/square     20    12    10     8     6     4     3
//     CHEMISTRY.md §6   —     —  1032   —     —    347    —
//     measured now   1419  1004   559    30    16    15     7
//
// Ten. It is the only value on that curve that is a *constraint* rather than a cull: about half
// the soup's carrying capacity, which is a population large enough to measure and small enough
// that matter is visibly what set it. Eight is already a cliff face — thirty cells — and six is
// sixteen, which is `the_drift.ron`'s problem in a different costume and unreadable for the same
// reason (§15.2).
//
// The old table should not be trusted anywhere else either, and CHEMISTRY.md §6 wants re-taking.
//
// `the_thicket.ron` also seeds low, at 40, and is doing something different and complementary:
// paired with `fluid_interval: 8` it makes carbon locally depletable inside a pack while the
// global pool stays large. That is a gradient across a crowd. This is a ceiling on the whole
// slide, and the two want keeping apart.
(
    name: "the lean water",
    seed: 20260812,
    width: 64,
    height: 64,

    // The control's light and water exactly: this slide is about matter and nothing else.
    light: Uniform(intensity: 1024),
    current: Still,
    fluid_interval: 1,

    seeding: [
        // Carbon dioxide and oxidant as the soup has them — photosynthesis is not what is being
        // limited here, and starving both at once would confound the two.
        Uniform(chemical: 11, per_square: 409600),
        // The carbonate system (`docs/CHEMISTRY.md` §11). Carbonate matched to the dissolved
        // CO2 above, so the slide starts at pH 7 and every move from there is something the
        // cells did. Calcium is then *not* free: the pair precipitates on the product of the
        // two, so this is set to put `sqrt(calcium * carbonate)` a little over
        // `minerals.calcite_saturation` — near enough to equilibrium that the pH decides which
        // way it goes, which is the whole point of the coupling.
        Uniform(chemical: 18, per_square: 409600),
        Uniform(chemical: 17, per_square: 3461),
        Uniform(chemical: 14, per_square: 409600),

        // Ten units a square. The soup's is 400.
        Uniform(chemical: 4, per_square: 10240),
        // The three minerals nothing in the engine produces (`docs/CHEMISTRY.md` §8): seeding is
        // the only way in, and without them a nucleus, an enzyme or a shell cannot be built at
        // all. At the Redfield proportion of this world's own carbon — 16/106 nitrogen, 1/106
        // phosphorus rounded up — and half that again in silicon, matching the fresh slide.
        Uniform(chemical: 5, per_square: 2048),
        Uniform(chemical: 6, per_square: 1024),
        // The inert pool a diazosome cracks. Four times the bioavailable nitrogen: a
        // young world is mostly locked up, and unlocking it is what the organelle is for.
        Uniform(chemical: 16, per_square: 8192),
        Uniform(chemical: 7, per_square: 5120),
    ],
    barriers: [],
)
